# AlertMind assistant — provider configuration.
#
# HOW TO USE: copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and fill in what you need.
#   cp .env.example .env          # macOS/Linux
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env   # PowerShell
# llm.py loads `.env` automatically on import. Variables already set in your
# shell take precedence over this file. `.env` is gitignored — never commit keys.
# The default `mock` provider needs none of these.

# --- Ollama (local, OpenAI-compatible; no key required) ---
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# Per-run Ollama sampling controls. When unset, AlertMind preserves the
# submitted llama3.1 request behavior (temperature=0; remaining model defaults).
# The following values are the selected Qwen3:8b provenance-rerun configuration:
# ALERTMIND_OLLAMA_TEMPERATURE=0.6
# ALERTMIND_OLLAMA_TOP_P=0.95
# ALERTMIND_OLLAMA_SEED=42
# ALERTMIND_OLLAMA_STRUCTURED_OUTPUTS=1
# Qwen's top_k=20 and repeat_penalty=1 remain model defaults because Ollama's
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint does not expose them as request fields. Preserve
# `ollama show qwen3:8b` output with the run evidence instead of claiming they
# were sent by AlertMind.
# Start llama3.1 or hosted-provider reruns from a clean shell (or explicitly
# clear these ALERTMIND_OLLAMA_* overrides) so Qwen settings cannot leak into a
# different comparison condition.

# --- NVIDIA build.nvidia.com (OpenAI-compatible, GPU-hosted) ---
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=nvapi-xxxxx

# --- OpenAI ---
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxx

# --- Anthropic ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxx

# Base URLs must stop at the API root (`.../v1`). Do not append `/responses`
# or `/chat/completions`; the client selects and appends the endpoint.
# Older configurations that used OPENAI_BASE_URL for Ollama still work, but
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL is preferred so switching providers cannot leak a stale URL.
# Run `python preflight.py --provider openai --model <model>` to verify.

# --- Reliability / performance (optional) ---
# ALERTMIND_LLM_TIMEOUT=300     # per-call seconds; raise for large local models
# ALERTMIND_MAX_TOKENS=1024     # cap response length (also speeds up local models)
# For the Qwen3 provenance reruns use timeout=900 and max_tokens=4096. Raise
# only max_tokens to 8192 if a diagnostic run still ends with finish_reason=length.
# ALERTMIND_LLM_RETRIES=2       # retries on transient errors (429/5xx/connection)
# ALERTMIND_OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=          # UNSET by default = vendor default (gpt-5.5: medium).
#                                             # gpt-5.5 supports: none|low|medium|high|xhigh.
#                                             # Setting "none" changes the inference config and may
#                                             # reduce multi-step triage quality — disclose if used.
#                                             # Reasoning tokens consume ALERTMIND_MAX_TOKENS.
